payload.description:
Every Papyrus feature epic ends with a docs page on the marketing and docs site, p.apyr.us (Papyrus-web).

Add pages covering multilingual copy-editing as it ships:
- Humanus language packs (Spanish and Chinese built together), typography fixed by code, and what "not supported" means for a language with no pack;
- the source-against-translation checks and the glossary / do-not-translate list;
- the `papyrus.story.localize` procedure: the convergence loop in which the machine rewrites its own translation and re-checks it against the English, never touching wording a person corrected;
- stock phrasing reported back on the English Story;
- target-locale conventions through the per-language glossary and pack, never omitting or altering a factual claim;
- how quality is evaluated: automated measures only (held-out set, per-language regression suite, bilingual model judges, parity, back-translation as a reading aid), with the plain statement that nobody in-house can verify Chinese quality so the measures are proxies;
- a rule may drive rewrites only at about 9 in 10 correct on held-out examples, measured per language;
- the `papyrus stories localize` CLI and the language quality page.

The Papyrus marketing website redesign session owns Papyrus-web. Coordinate with it before editing. Source: docs/plans/multilingual-publishing.md, ~/Projects/papyrus-multilingual-humanus-design.md.

Acceptance: the pages are live on p.apyr.us, linked from the docs index, and accurate to the released version.
